<DocsLayout title="Step 5 automatic verification" description="Use RelayBridge's bounded Step-5 verification session when the exact eligible Exchange SMTP 535 condition persists after validated administration." section="Microsoft 365">
  <section>
    <h2>Propagation is possible, not assumed</h2>
    <p>New Exchange authorization may take time to become effective. RelayBridge treats propagation as one possibility after validated administration; it does not classify every SMTP 535 as propagation and does not promise a completion time.</p>
    <p>For the exact eligible Step 5 SMTP authentication denial, RelayBridge first performs up to four total attempts: the initial attempt, then retries after 2, 5, and 10 seconds while the same eligible condition persists.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Automatic session limits</h2>
    <p>If the short bounded sequence still receives the eligible SMTP 535, the active Step 5 page can start an automatic verification session.</p>
    <div class="docs-table-wrap">
      <table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Released behavior</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Interval</th><td>Every five minutes</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Attempt limit</th><td>12 automatic attempts</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Elapsed limit</th><td>One hour</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Check now</th><td>Schedules one immediate check in the same session without overlapping work</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Stop automatic checks</th><td>Stops future verification checks without canceling the setup candidate</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Leave or close page</th><td>Disposes the page-scoped session and cancels its future checks</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Candidate change</th><td>The session cannot adopt or activate a different candidate</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What each attempt does</h2>
    <p>Every attempt revalidates the candidate identity, revision, and fingerprint. It uses the existing certificate and application identity, performs no tenant mutation or permission broadening, and requires no additional administrator authentication.</p>
    <p>While authentication is rejected, RelayBridge sends no <code>MAIL</code>, <code>RCPT</code>, or <code>DATA</code>. Once authentication succeeds, the normal verification path performs the existing final acceptance test and atomically activates the candidate.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>If verification expires</h2>
    <p>Use the displayed safe error and Diagnostics to review tenant and mailbox SMTP AUTH policy, application identity, certificate validity, the Exchange service-principal reference, and effective RBAC scope.</p>
    <div class="docs-callout">
      <strong>Do not weaken the boundary</strong>
      <p>Do not enable Basic Auth, grant broad Graph mail permissions, disable TLS validation, replace the candidate during an active session, or retry every SMTP 535 indefinitely.</p>
    </div>
